{"name":"Fun and Games","hex":"#33789c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fun and games","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Recreation; nothing serious; easy, enjoyable activities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fun_and_games"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fun and Games (The Huntingtons album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fun and Games is an album by the Huntingtons released in 1997 on Flying Tart Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5e/Hunt-fungames.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fun_and_Games_(The_Huntingtons_album)","wikidata":"Q5508693"},{"title":"Fun & Games (The Connells album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fun & Games is the third studio album by the American band the Connells, released in 1989. It was recorded primarily at Fort Apache Studios, in Cambridge, MA, with additional recording at Studio 900 in New York City and Reflection Studio in Charlotte, NC."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/09/Fun%26games.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fun_%26_Games_(The_Connells_album)","wikidata":"Q5508635"},{"title":"Fun and Games (Better Call Saul)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Fun and Games\" is the ninth episode of the sixth season of Better Call Saul, the spin-off television series of Breaking Bad. It was directed by Michael Morris and written by Ann Cherkis. The episode aired on AMC and AMC+ on July 18, 2022, before debuting online in certain territories on Netflix the following day. In the episode, Gus Fring discusses the death of Lalo Salamanca with the cartel, Mike Ehrmantraut ties up a loose end, and Jimmy McGill and Kim Wexler deal with the aftermath of Howard Hamlin's murder."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/Fun_and_Games_promo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnai